[2026-09-21 14:51:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 080]   Step 080 -- signed residual coherence: precession vs anomaly.
[2026-09-21 14:51:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 080]   Step 075 found the catalogue signed rotation directionally coherent
[2026-09-21 14:51:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 080]   on both catalogues, but with a population-wide sign bias (70-84% one
[2026-09-21 14:51:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 080]   sign).  The mundane source of a global bias is secular omega
[2026-09-21 14:51:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 080]   precession by the giant planets across the ~600 yr leg separation --
[2026-09-21 14:51:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 080]   a real, directed torque.  This step measures the SIGNED rotation the
[2026-09-21 14:51:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 080]   N-body planets themselves produce on the same bidirectional legs
[2026-09-21 14:51:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 080]   (shell 250 AU, step-063 convention), subtracts it from the catalogue
[2026-09-21 14:51:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 080]   signed rotation, and asks whether the residual sign remains coherent
[2026-09-21 14:51:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 080]   in-cap.  If the in-cap sign coherence survives subtraction it is a
[2026-09-21 14:51:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 080]   directed phase structure beyond the planets; if it collapses to
[2026-09-21 14:51:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 080]   50/50 the sign was planetary.
